--seam-check-cost: one `seam-check-cost:` line per checked firing, the z3
rlimit count and the time of its query. The count is in the unit
--seam-check-rlimit enforces: the costliest firing is decided at twice its
count and runs out (reason=rlimit) at a tenth (Inputs/check-cost.py).
RUN: sea-vc %S/row-group.mlir --lower --solver=z3 --seam --seam-check --seam-check-cost | FileCheck %s
CHECK: seam-check-cost: id={{[0-9]+}} rlimit={{[0-9]+}} time={{[0-9]+\.[0-9]+}}
CHECK: seam-check: firings={{[0-9]+}}
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-cost.py sea-vc %S/row-group.mlir --lower --solver=z3 --seam | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RL
RL: check-cost: ok

Off by default: the output of --seam-check is unchanged.
RUN: sea-vc %S/row-group.mlir --lower --solver=z3 --seam --seam-check | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OFF
OFF-NOT: seam-check-cost
OFF: seam-check: firings=

Without --seam-check it is an error.
RUN: not sea-vc %S/row-group.mlir --lower --seam --seam-check-cost 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ERR
ERR: --seam-check-cost needs --seam-check

Another backend has no rlimit count: `-`.
RUN: %if bitwuzla %{ sea-vc %S/row-group.mlir --lower --solver=bitwuzla --seam --seam-check --seam-check-cost | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BZ %}
BZ: seam-check-cost: id={{[0-9]+}} rlimit=- time=
RUN: %if yices %{ sea-vc %S/row-group.mlir --lower --solver=yices --seam --seam-check --seam-check-cost | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BZ %}

